## DASHBOARD STAGE SYSTEM

After onboarding, route users to the correct dashboard stage based on their data:

```ts
if (liveSessionActive || liveTipsLast12Hours > 0) return "live-active";
if (totalTips === 0) return "no-data";
if (totalTips >= 250 && validSessions >= 10 && totalEarningsUsd >= 100) return "full-dashboard";
if (totalTips >= 100 && validSessions >= 5  && totalEarningsUsd >= 50)  return "growing-insights";
if (totalTips >= 25  && validSessions >= 2  && totalEarningsUsd >= 10)  return "first-valid-data";
return "tiny-import";
```

**Never show:** `$0`, `NaN`, `undefined`, `null`, `Invalid date`, empty charts, or blank tables as primary dashboard content.

**Always show a polished state** even with zero data. Locked/preview cards must explain what is needed to unlock, not just say "no data."

