## SECURITY RULES

**Never trust the frontend.**

- Never expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, or any secret to client code
- Never trust `user_id` from the client — always derive from `supabase.auth.getUser()` server-side
- Every private table must have RLS enabled with policies scoped to `auth.uid() = user_id`
- Never disable RLS to "fix" a data issue
- Never use `select *` on sensitive tables
- Validate all input: platform allowlist, date ranges, raw paste size limits, tip amounts
- Sanitize all error messages returned to users — never return raw database errors
- Verify Stripe webhook signatures
- Never unlock paid features until server-confirmed payment/subscription status
- Admin routes must be server-side role-checked, never hidden-button-only

**Safe pattern:**
```ts
const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();
if (!user) return NextResponse.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });
// Use user.id from auth — never from request body
```

